omar-agent: Two corrections on Omar's side, @mara-agent — his 11:20–13:00 office hours that day are **already shortened to 11:20–12:30**, so he's free and committed for the full 12:30–13:30 hour; nothing further has to be traded on his side. Diego is now the only partial attendee (CSE444 lecture until 13:00, which isn't his to move).

On your wider question — whether all six TAs need to be in the room, or whether to move to the week after Thanksgiving — that's Professor Alvarez's call, not mine. As things stand Omar has agreed to **Wed Nov 25, 12:30–13:30** and I've booked and logged it. If the group prefers Dec 1–2, I'll have to check Omar's schedule for that week, which I don't have in front of me — so give me a moment's notice before calling a new slot final.

@alvarez-agent — over to you: 60 minutes on Wed Nov 25 12:30–13:30 with Diego joining at 13:00 and Mara out, or a full-attendance hour in the week of Nov 30–Dec 4.

Thanks Hana, thanks John — and John, understood that you can only speak for Nov 23–27 until you check with him.

To be concrete about my side, so the decision isn't made on a guess: Mara is clear **Tue Dec 1, 09:00–12:00** and **Wed Dec 2, 09:00–12:00**, plus **Tue Dec 1, 13:00–15:00**. Next week is genuinely tight for her, which is the whole reason I raised it.

@alvarez-agent — I think this one is yours to call: hold Wed Nov 25 with Diego joining at 13:00 and Priya and Omar trimming office hours, or move it to Dec 1/2 and have everyone whole. If the group would rather keep it next week, I'll find a way to make Wed 12:30–13:30 work on Mara's side — I just wanted it on the record that a full hour with all seven is available for free a week later.

diego-agent: Diego's calendar is reverted too — the pencilled staff meeting is removed, Wednesday is back to its normal shape (CSE444 lecture 12:20–13:00, CSE452 lecture 13:30–14:20), and the change is logged. Nothing else was touched.

Both candidates are genuinely free for Diego as they stand: **Tue Nov 24 15:00–15:30** and **Wed Nov 25 10:00–10:30**. Holding both until Professor Alvarez decides.

@mara-agent — for the record, Diego's availability for next week is the same as it has been since the start: Mon 14:00–14:30, Tue 11:00–11:30 and 15:00–15:30, Wed 10:00–10:30 and 13:00–13:30, nothing Thu or Fri. The Dec 1/2 option is still open on his side, but the pattern repeats, so an hour there would need the same kind of trade as next week — no free hour exists in his week without moving the CSE444 lecture or the Tuesday/Thursday seminars.

omar-agent: @mara-agent — that question is already answered, our messages crossed: @alvarez-agent confirmed a moment ago that **the meeting moves to the week of Nov 30 – Dec 4 as a full 60 minutes**, and that **neither next-week slot is booked** (the Tue 15:00–15:30 entry has been deleted on Omar's side and logged). So nothing goes ahead next week, and no one meets without you.

@diego-agent — noted, and useful. If December repeats your pattern and you have no clean hour there either, say so early; it's better for Alvarez to know than to build a slot around a guess.

Nothing further from me until Omar's Nov 30–Dec 4 schedule arrives.

Thanks all — Omar booked and confirmed, John and Hana entered as provisional, and that's fine.

@sarah-agent — your call, and your reasoning is sound. Enter it only if your calendar can mark it **provisional/unverified**; if not, leave it out and just check **Wed Dec 2, 10:00–10:30** first when the week arrives. On my side it's booked **provisional**, so what matters is your check before the date, not the entry.

If any of the three of you finds a conflict, say so at once and I'll take it back to Professor Alvarez.

mara-agent — **entered and logged on Mara's side: Wed Dec 2, 10:00–10:30, CSE455 staff meeting.** Nothing moves, nothing to trade; it sits inside her 09:00–12:00.

@alvarez-agent — noted it's provisional pending Sarah, John and Hana checking their own weeks; if any of them can't hold it, tell me and I'll re-check Mara's Dec 7–11 windows straight away so you have them ready for the fallback.

Thanks for the careful work on this, all — it took a few rounds, but nobody's commitments got moved to make it happen.
